d reduced attack surface; Zero Trust Browser, a solution that secures browser-based access to business applications for the extended workforce, including third parties and partners; Zscaler Digital Experience, a solution that monitors end-user experience and helps organizations identify and resolve performance issues across their digital environment; Zero Trust Branch; and Zero Trust Cloud solutions. It also provides Security for AI solution to secure AI adoption across the full AI ecosystem; data security services, including AI-powered data classification and contextual insights, data loss prevention, Saas security, and data security posture management solution. In addition, the company offers Agentic Security Operations solution that enables enterprises to reduce cyber risk by using AI-powered automation; exposure management platform; deception; managed detection and response; agentic security operations center; and threat hunting solutions. It serves automotive, airlines and transportation, conglomerates, consumer goods and retail, energy, financial services, healthcare, insurance, manufacturing, media and communications, public sector and education, technology, and telecommunications services industries. The company was formerly known as SafeChannel, Inc. and changed its name to Zscaler, Inc. in August 2008. Zscaler, Inc. was incorporated in 2007 and is headquartered in Santa Clara, California.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Jagtar Singh Chaudhry | Co-Founder, CEO & Chairman of the Board | Age 66 | Compensation: $29,753 (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 8K people. Revenue per employee of $385K ranks in the above the sector median among Technology peers, with revenue growing 43%/yr across its filed history. Each employee generates $98K of free cash flow annually. Stock-based compensation of $94K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 0\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags moderate compensation governance risk (6/10).","financial_summary":["Zscaler, Inc. is a large-cap technology business with a $31.4B market cap on $3.4B of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at +28% over the past three years, the kind of sustained demand persistence that marks a compounder.","Returns on capital run at -28% against a 12% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests. Gross margins of 78% confirm genuine pricing power.","The business throws off $852M in free cash flow \u2014 roughly 25 cents on every revenue dollar, which is the owner-earnings figure that actually belongs to shareholders.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year, and thin -11.3\u00d7 interest coverage leaves no room for a bad year.","Shareholder yield is only 0.0%, a thin return of capital, and stock-based comp at 25% of revenue is silent dilution an owner has to account for, and insiders hold 35% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is, and profit capture is only 0.0\u00d7 the fair share, suggesting no structural edge inside its industry."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 615% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":6.146985597448673},{"text":"Piotroski score 3/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Operating margins 11% below sector median \u2014 a cost disadvantage the moat cannot hide","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Above-average short interest at 5.5% of float","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $11.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Financial quality metrics lag Technology peers","sev":"amber","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 7% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (38% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Founder-led \u2014 owner alignment that often matters more than any incentive plan","Gross margin tops the Technology peer set \u2014 genuine pricing power is present here","Growing faster than most Technology peers \u2014 taking share inside the profit pool","Among the least levered in Technology \u2014 the fortress balance sheet in its peer set"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Zscaler, Inc. $ZS Position Cut by Keybank National Association OH","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/13/zscaler-inc-zs-position-cut-by-keybank-national-association-oh.html","date":"2026-11-13","timestamp":1794564210.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.818,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Will AI Security Partnership Change Zscaler (ZS) Stock Narrative","source":"simplywall.st","link":"https://simplywall.st/stocks/us/software/nasdaq-zs/zscaler/news/will-ai-security-partnership-change-zscaler-zs-stock-narrati","date":"2026-11-12","timestamp":1794482921.596,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.932,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["product"]},{"title":"Machina Capital S.A.S. Acquires 3,748 Shares of Zscaler, Inc. $ZS","source":"thelincolnia